cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this candidate, its ephemeris or this code, please cite it as below."
title: "TIC 149928372.01: a 2.7 Earth-radius, 16.36-day transiting planet candidate around the M dwarf TIC 149928372"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Paliwal
    given-names: Advait
    email: advaitpaliwal@gmail.com
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/advaitpaliwal/TIC149928372"
url: "https://github.com/advaitpaliwal/TIC149928372"
abstract: >-
  A transit-like signal on TIC 149928372, an early M dwarf at 79 pc, found on
  2026-10-23 in TESS photometry from Sectors 14, 21, 41, 47, 48, 74 and 75.
  Period 16.364477 +/- 0.000035 d, mid-transit BJD_TDB 2459518.8453 +/- 0.0013,
  depth about 1450 ppm, duration 3.36 h, impact parameter 0.37, radius
  2.67 (+0.29/-0.28) Earth radii, insolation 8.7 times Earth's. Difference
  images in all seven sectors place the dip on the target. False-positive
  probability 0.0169 +/- 0.0035 without companion limits and 0.0019 +/- 0.0017
  with MOLUSC Gaia companion limits, no neighbours removed; high-resolution
  imaging not checked, so a planet candidate, not a validated planet.
keywords:
  - exoplanet
  - transit
  - TESS
  - planet candidate
  - M dwarf
  - TIC 149928372
